WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:08.750
In March 1948 Pauling was on his back in Oxford with a sinus infection, reading

2
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.850
mystery novels until they bored him.

3
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.330
Then he asked his wife to bring him paper and a slide rule.

4
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:20.240
He drew a polypeptide chain at the right scale, kept every peptide bond flat the way

5
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.280
the chemistry demanded, and folded the strip until it wound onto itself a right

6
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:32.420
-handed coil, 3.6 residues per turn, every backbone NH hydrogen bonded to a CO4

7
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.420
residues back.

8
00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:39.913
He noticed the rise per turn came out near 5.4 angstroms, not quite the 5.1

9
00:00:39.913 --> 00:00:44.133
measured for keratin, and let the discrepancy stand rather than bend the chemistry

10
00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.133
to fit it.

11
00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:50.047
He had taught the world to deduce a structure from the bonds alone and four years

12
00:00:50.047 --> 00:00:54.687
later the State Department refused to renew his passport, keeping him out of London

13
00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.647
where the DNA photographs waited.

14
00:00:57.327 --> 00:01:01.747
The man who could read structure from first principles missed the structure of the

15
00:01:01.747 --> 00:01:02.007
gene.
